isofill (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The second pass out of core is the second pass. Above --max-mem it was
    a banded approximation - a coarse grid solved whole, then each band of
    rows against it, the margins pinned to the coarse answer and the void
    decided on the coarse grid - and it was wrong by hundreds of metres: on
    zone-ellarca 310,572 cells off by more than 100 m, up to 1,933 m, every
    large error on a band join or in enclosed ground taken for void.
  * Now the same solve runs over the same arrays, and those that will not
    fit in what is left of --max-mem are kept in files beside the output,
    mapped into memory and unlinked as they are made. Every step reads rows
    in order or tiles of them, so the kernel pages a pass over each file.
    The answer is the whole raster's to the bit: identical on zone-ellarca
    at 3", gobras at 1" in a cgroup capped at 1.2 GB against 2.1 GB of
    arrays, and zone-yuethon at 3" - at about the banded path's time.
  * --pass2-margin is accepted and ignored; it was the bands' overlap.
  * tests/pass2_ooc in make check: the binary run whole and with
    --max-mem 1 on a raster with void, sea and enclosed unreached ground,
    every cell compared.

 -- Lee Kindness <wangi@opengeofiction.net>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:44:27 +0100

